    "code_l_label": false,
    "how_b_and_w_are_rows": "Code W is the covered-w family, itemized as wash-sale proceeds, basis, and adjustment, and posted to Schedule D lines 1b and 8b. Code B is the code-b family, itemized under labels that say code B, with column (g) the recorded basis correction plus any wash, and posted to the same lines. Covered sales with no wash and no code B stay on lines 1a and 8a and are not itemized on the attachment.",
    "how_other_codes_are_refused": "The filer must answer that every Form 8949 sale is a broker-reported basis sale with no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss or a code B basis correction, or a box B, C, E, or F securities sale with no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss. The fact no-other-form8949-adjustments is titled as no adjustment code other than W, no multi-code row, and no basis-not-reported source. A code L row is none of those, so the honest answer is no, and the return stays refused. There is no code L family.",
