      "fact_type": "tax.us.2025.f1099b.statement-box7-loss-not-allowed",
      "text": "For each Form 1099-B or substitute statement you recorded a sale from, is box 7 (\"If checked, loss is not allowed based on amount in 1d\") checked for any sale on it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "tax.us.2025.input-question.schedule-d-boundary-form8949-code-b-in-class",
      "version": "v1",
      "adopted_on_v85": true,
      "fact_type": "tax.us.2025.schedule-d-boundary.form8949-code-b-in-class",
      "text": "Each sale on your Form 8949 should be one of two kinds. (1) A sale your broker reported to the IRS with its basis, with no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss or a correction of that basis. (2) A sale of stocks or other securities, entered only once and in the one box its statement gives it, with a basis you supply (the correct basis, even if your Form 1099-B showed a different one), net proceeds you supply when you got no Form 1099-B, and no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss. Is every sale on your Form 8949 one of these two kinds?"
    },
    {
      "id": "tax.us.2025.input-question.schedule-d-boundary-form8949-in-class",
      "version": "v1",
      "adopted_on_v85": true,
      "fact_type": "tax.us.2025.schedule-d-boundary.form8949-in-class",
      "text": "Is every sale on your Form 8949 either a sale your broker reported with its basis and no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss, or a sale of stocks or other securities, entered only once, with a basis you supply (and net proceeds you supply when you got no Form 1099-B) and no adjustment other than a wash-sale loss?"
    }
  ]
